&lt;ul style=&quot;&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Optical Mark Reader (OMR) can be considered as a&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;Scanning device.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Optical mark recognition is the process of&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;capturing human-marked data&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;from document forms such as&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;surveys and tests.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;They are used to&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;read questionnaires&lt;/span&gt;, and multiple-choice examination papers in the form of&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;shaded areas.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;An OMR scanner can maintain a throughput of&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;2000 to 10,000&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;forms per hour.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

